# Linear merge notification (page/template location)

## Trigger

Check this after commits land on a working branch, and especially right after a merge to **`main`**:

1. The current branch name contains a Linear issue key (`[A-Z]+-\d+`, e.g. `PP-1234`).
2. Either:
   - there are commits on this branch not yet on `main` (work in progress on this issue), or
   - this branch's commits are now reachable from `main` (`git merge-base --is-ancestor <branch> main`) — the work just landed.

If neither holds, this rule does not apply — skip silently.

## Dismiss / snooze first

Before notifying, read **`.assistant-setup/linear-merge-notification.local.json`** (gitignored local state) if it exists, and look up the entry for the current issue key:

| Stored `mode` | Skip notifying when |
|---|---|
| `next-commit` | `atSha` still equals the branch's current HEAD (no new commit landed since the user dismissed it) |
| `next-merge` | the branch still isn't merged into `main` yet |
| `this-issue` | always, for this issue key — until the user explicitly asks to re-enable it |

If the stored condition has since been satisfied (a new commit landed, or the merge happened), **delete that entry** and proceed with the notification below as normal — dismissals are one-shot per condition, not permanent unless `this-issue` was chosen.

When you notify (below) and the user wants to postpone instead of acting now, ask which of the three options they want and write/update the entry, e.g.:

```json
{
  "PP-1234": { "mode": "next-commit", "atSha": "<current branch HEAD sha>" }
}
```

`next-merge` and `this-issue` entries omit `atSha`. Create the file if it doesn't exist, and add `.assistant-setup/linear-merge-notification.local.json` to `.gitignore` if it isn't already ignored — this is local scratch state, not shared repo history.

## What to notify

Tell the user where the Portal Page / template behind this repo lives:

- **Identity:** `mi.url` + `app.id` from `pp-dev.config.ts` (or `pp-dev.config`; pre-1.0 `pp-dev`: `backendBaseURL` + `portalPageId`). `app.type` tells you whether this is a `'template'` (syncs back to MI) or a standalone `'page'`.
- **Edit / view links:** use whatever is already recorded under **Routes and Page Flows → MI page location** in **`.assistant-setup/page-workflow-context.md`**. If the edit/view URLs for this page aren't recorded yet, build them from the URL patterns in that section (look up the template id with `GET <mi.url>/api/page/id/<page-id>`); if the instance version doesn't match those patterns, ask the user or check **`.dev-environment.md`** rather than guessing. Record them in `page-workflow-context.md` once known so this and future runs don't have to re-derive them.

## Suggest a Linear comment

If **`linear-cli`** is configured (`linear-cli auth status`, or a successful `linear-cli i get <ISSUE_KEY>`):

1. Check existing comments on the issue itself and on directly related issues (parent/sub-issues, linked duplicates) for a links comment in the format below with the current URLs. If found, don't suggest posting again — just mention it's already there. Links buried in another comment or hidden behind labels don't count; offer the separate comment anyway.
2. Otherwise, propose posting the links comment below and **ask before posting** — see **`.cursor/skills/linear-workflow/SKILL.md`** for `linear-cli i comment`. Never post automatically.

### Links comment format

This follows the team's Ready to Test checklist (https://wiki.mtrc.in/doc/ready-to-test-checklist-TMcZPWcJ6J). Before moving the issue to **Ready to Test**, the PR is merged into the target branch, all assets are updated, and the change is verified on the real server, not only locally.

- Post the links as **their own comment**. Don't put them inside a release summary, QA report or any other comment.
- Write every link as the **full plain URL**. Don't hide it behind a markdown label (`[view](…)`, `[edit](…)`), so the reader sees exactly where each one goes.
- Use these four labels, in this order and spelled like this:

```markdown
**Repository (Repo):** https://github.com/<org>/<repo>

**Template:** <mi.url>/editor/page/template/<template-id>

**App Editor:** <mi.url>/editor/page/<page-id>

**Application (App):** <mi.url>/p/<internal-name>
```

- **Repository** is the `origin` remote as an `https://github.com/...` URL. **Template**, **App Editor** and **Application** come from **MI page location** in `page-workflow-context.md`; on instances before 7.0, **App Editor** is the legacy admin URL. For a standalone `'page'` with no template, write `**Template:** none (standalone page)`.
- Notes for QA (known limitations, testing steps, feature flags, dependencies) go after the four links in the same comment, as plain text. Leave them out when there is nothing to add.

